  "id": "cornerthemarket",
  "neon": "#ffe08a",
  "note": "CORNER THE MARKET — the corner shop on Filament Street.\n\nThe tile's prose: a shopfront of adverts layered so deep that the actual window is down to a\nletterbox of clear glass at head height; crates of whatever is going out on the pavement under an\nawning that winds down with a handle; open at six and not clearly ever closed.\n\nSo the ground floor is a wall of advert boards in two rows, with the letterbox window above them\nand the door at the end, under a wind-down awning with crates in front. The name is on the fascia.\nIt used to draw on the `bodega` type arm, which lettered every bodega BODEGA VU.",
